# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# holiday-planning — a group holiday decision app. Onboarded 2026-10-29.
#
#   "Can we onboard holiday app onto kit, I am going to add this with my first
#   test user. This will be a shared repo so my bot can actually pick up the new
#   items. Will have to implement a different mechanism for the testers own
#   projects. Ai api most likely"
#                                     — his note in Kit, 2026-10-29 08:09Z
#
# Read at holiday-planning@dev a050752 (dev and main were both read; dev is ahead
# and is where work lands). What exists is a .NET backend only: the Compromise
# Engine (a deterministic scorer that ranks holiday options against a group's
# preferences and dealbreakers) behind four trip routes and a status route.
# docs/DESIGN.md is the product spec it was built from. The frontend is still the
# unmodified web-template placeholder (one Home page, no holiday screens), so no
# behaviour below is a page and none is invented for one.
#
#   DEFINED   — his words. Cites the note.
#   INFERRED  — what the backend already does, read off the code. Cites file:line.
#               Each is `review unreviewed`, so it shows in Proposed and he can
#               deny it.
#
# Not here, on purpose: the chat decision feed, reactions, auth, real flight/hotel
# data and LLM features. docs/DESIGN.md sketches them as later slices; he has not
# asked for them in Kit, so they are not behaviours yet.
#
# Promotion to main stays his: no grant names this project.
#
# kit:repo jemmy8oy-northstar/holiday-planning@dev
#   BEH-HEALTH-1: where this app's tests live. Hosted Kit reads them from there to count coverage.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

feature FEAT-PROJECT "How this project is worked"
  stage development
feature FEAT-TRIP "Trips and the people in them"
  stage development
feature FEAT-ENGINE "The Compromise Engine: ranked options with reasons"
  stage development
feature FEAT-STATUS "What the service says about itself"
  stage development


# ═══ DEFINED — his notes ═══

behaviour BEH-SHARE-1 "The project is shared with his first test user, and the bot picks up its items like any Kit project"
  in FEAT-PROJECT
  layer technical
  source defined kit.notes.md#2026-10-29-0809
  review approved
  priority 2
  actor owner
  contract "This will be a shared repo so my bot can actually pick up the new items"
  contract my assumption: the test user's items on this repo reach the bot the way any Kit project's do, through the Kit spec and its Queue
  contract not built here: "Will have to implement a different mechanism for the testers own projects. Ai api most likely" is about the tester's own projects, which are not this repo, and is left for him to spec
  contract my reading of the answer posted on 2026-11-02 at 17:53Z (holiday-planning.notes.md#2026-11-02-1753): it is the chat agent's summary of this card, posted from the chat, not an answer to whether the access was given, so the question below stands with its default
  contract built 2026-11-05, his default taken on silence: the bot half is done (holiday-planning is on Kit and its Queue reaches the bot); giving his test user access to the repo and to Kit stays his, off the board


# ═══ INFERRED — what the backend already does ═══

behaviour BEH-TRIP-1 "A person creates a trip by giving it a name"
  in FEAT-TRIP
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.WebApi/Routes/TripRoutes.cs:19
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract POST /api/trips returns 201 with the new trip's id, name and creation time
  contract a blank name is refused with 400; the name is trimmed before it is stored

behaviour BEH-TRIP-2 "A person adds a member to a trip with their vibe preferences and dealbreakers"
  in FEAT-TRIP
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.WebApi/Routes/TripRoutes.cs:44
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract POST /api/trips/{id}/members takes a display name, vibe weights and dealbreakers; a blank display name is refused with 400
  contract a trip that does not exist answers 404
  contract the three dealbreaker types are budget_per_person_above, travel_hours_above and must_have_vibe; any other type is ignored when scoring

behaviour BEH-TRIP-3 "A person reads a trip and sees its members"
  in FEAT-TRIP
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.WebApi/Routes/TripRoutes.cs:30
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract GET /api/trips/{id} returns the trip with its members; a trip that does not exist answers 404

behaviour BEH-REC-1 "A trip's recommendations rank every option, viable ones first and blocked ones after"
  in FEAT-ENGINE
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.Services/RecommendationService.cs:27
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract GET /api/trips/{id}/recommendations scores every catalog option against all members; viable options come by group score descending, then blocked ones by group score descending
  contract a blocked option is never dropped, so the group can see what a relaxed constraint would unlock
  contract a trip that does not exist answers 404

behaviour BEH-REC-2 "A dealbreaker vetoes an option for that member and blocks it for the group"
  in FEAT-ENGINE
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.Services/OptionScoringService.cs:103
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract a member's fit is 0 and the option is blocked when the cost per person is over their budget, the travel is longer than their limit, or an option's intensity for their must-have vibe is under 0.5 (exactly 0.5 passes)
  contract the first failing dealbreaker gives the reason, which names the member and the numbers

behaviour BEH-REC-3 "A member's fit blends how well the vibes match with how comfortable the budget is"
  in FEAT-ENGINE
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.Services/OptionScoringService.cs:56
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract fit is 0.7 x vibe match plus 0.3 x budget comfort; vibe match is the weighted average of the option's vibe intensities under the member's weights
  contract budget comfort is the headroom under the member's budget, clamped to 0..1; a member with no stated vibes or no budget is neutral at 0.5

behaviour BEH-REC-4 "The group score favours options everyone likes over options some love and one hates"
  in FEAT-ENGINE
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.Services/OptionScoringService.cs:191
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract group score is 0.6 x the mean of member fits plus 0.4 x the lowest member fit; a vetoed member counts as 0

behaviour BEH-REC-5 "Every recommendation explains each member's fit in words"
  in FEAT-ENGINE
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.Services/OptionScoringService.cs:77
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract each member fit carries reasons: the top two matching vibes, a neutral note when they stated none, or the veto reason

behaviour BEH-REC-6 "The options come from a built-in catalog of ten example destinations"
  in FEAT-ENGINE
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.Services/OptionCatalogService.cs:16
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor traveller
  contract the catalog is fixed in code (Crete to Bali) with per-person GBP cost, travel hours, nights and vibe intensities; it is dummy data and is not stored

behaviour BEH-STATUS-1 "GET /api/status says which version is running and how it is doing"
  in FEAT-STATUS
  source inferred backend/HolidayPlanning.WebApi/Routes/StatusRoutes.cs:13
  review unreviewed
  priority 4
  actor engineer
